WEBVTT

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.370
Morning...

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:05.370
Let's eat!

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:13.260
To Kotori
From Mom

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:17.380
Morning!
I'll be on live TV at 7:15.
So nervous!
Good luck today!

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:19.180
"I'll be on live TV at 7:15."

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:23.430
Wait... Right now?

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.060
A live broadcast?

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.160
Monday, April 24th.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:31.360
It's now 7:15 AM.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.450
Tonight at 7:00 PM,

00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:39.520
we'll be having special guests on 
<i>Quiz Academy Smarty-Smarts Special!</i>

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:40.950
Good morning!

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:46.040
Watch!

00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:46.040
A Two-Hour Special Tonight at 7:00  
Quiz Academy Smarty-Smarts

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:43.900
<i>Kotori, are you watching?</i>

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:46.040
<b>Guest: Iida Megumi (Cooking Specialist)</b>

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.040
<i>Mom's gonna do her best, okay?</i>

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:23.470
<b>Tsumugi and the Long-Awaited Hamburg Steak</b>

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.040
Daddy's is burnt.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:33.270
I take responsibility for my failures.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:36.190
Let's eat.

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:39.390
How's the miso soup?

00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:40.760
It boiled a little,

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.900
but I remembered what we did with 
the pork soup when I flavored it...

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:48.840
The fried tofu is long!

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:52.240
That means you're a winner, Tsumugi.

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:53.120
You can win?

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:54.700
There are winners?!

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:56.840
Congratulations...

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.470
It's good!

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:15.350
Mr. Galigali is fluffy-fluffs!

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:21.130
Tsumugi, hold on a second.

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:29.740
There.

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:39.660
Daddy!

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:42.120
Thanks for cleaning up, Tsumugi.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:46.920
We'll do the rest when Daddy gets back, okay?

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:50.020
Oh, the papers!

00:04:57.130 --> 00:05:00.080
<b>April</b>

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:03.360
When I turned on the TV this morning,

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:05.980
my mom was in a sailor outfit.

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:06.680
Sheesh.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:08.660
That's wrong!

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.840
Seriously, that's just wrong!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:17.100
Honestly... Even if it's for TV, 
some things just aren't okay.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.960
Even I've never worn a sailor uniform!

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:23.710
And it looked pretty good on her, too!

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:26.760
Is that why your mom's busy?

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:29.370
Yes.

00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:32.730
It's not like she's a celebrity 
or anything, though.

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:35.600
Oh, how did breakfast go?

00:05:36.660 --> 00:05:39.260
I burned the scrambled eggs.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:43.440
B-But the miso soup turned out okay, right?

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:45.450
After I put the miso it,

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:48.160
I put it on the burner for a bit,
and it started boiling.

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.120
I used hot water to thin it out.

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:52.660
I see.

00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:56.440
Sensei, are you afraid of undercooking things?

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.360
I guess I am.

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:02.780
Tsumugi has a really rough time 
when she gets a stomachache.

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.100
Okay, everyone!

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:22.380
Tsumugi-chan!

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.110
Let's play!

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.090
Next time!

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.760
What're you doing?

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:30.610
I'm making a Hamburg steak!

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:32.910
This is Daddy's steak!

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.460
I made one, and now I don't have enough clay

00:06:44.460 --> 00:06:47.660
to make the plates and chopsticks and spoon.

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:49.660
Oh, no!

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:51.180
Yeah!

00:06:51.480 --> 00:06:52.600
Here you go.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.760
It's okay. You can use mine.

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:57.790
Mine, too.

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:00.010
Really? I can?

00:07:00.010 --> 00:07:02.810
We haven't played with clay 
for a while, so it's okay.

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:04.680
Thank you!

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:09.450
Everyone, let's start cleaning up.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:11.100
Okay!

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:18.250
Tsumugi-chan, you're coming 
to my house today, right?

00:07:18.580 --> 00:07:22.490
Yeah! Daddy said I could!

00:07:23.640 --> 00:07:26.920
Ts-Tsumugi-chan, isn't that heavy?

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:28.030
It's okay!

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:31.370
Oh, where'd you get all that clay?

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.510
It was a present!

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.000
No fair!

00:07:35.790 --> 00:07:39.980
Sensei, she took clay from other kids!

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.680
No, I didn't! They gave it to me!

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:43.530
Right?

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:44.610
Yeah.

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.670
But it's not fair that she 
gets it all to herself!

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:49.610
Right?

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:52.580
They gave it to me, so it's mine now!

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:55.210
You're not gonna give it back?

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:57.350
That makes you a thief!

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:02.580
<b>30,000 quick recipes! 
No cooking skills required!</b>

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:02.580
<b>Keyword Search</b>

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.580
<b>Hamburg Steak</b>

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:08.670
Inuzuka-sensei.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:10.190
Yes?

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:12.110
Did something good happen?

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:14.800
Huh? No... why?

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:16.470
Just a hunch.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:21.820
Yes, this is Inuzuka.

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:23.130
Yes.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.120
What?

00:08:26.630 --> 00:08:28.770
I'm sorry. Okay.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:30.820
I'll come get her.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:32.910
Sure. See you soon.

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:35.700
What's wrong?

00:08:37.670 --> 00:08:40.790
It seems my daughter 
got into a bit of trouble.

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:45.000
Tsumugi!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.850
Sorry to call you out here 
like this, Inuzuka-san.

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:49.310
No, it's fine.

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:51.480
So where are Tsumugi and Mikio-kun?

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:52.710
Over there.

00:08:59.380 --> 00:09:01.760
Tsumugi-chan scratched me!

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:03.770
Did not!

00:09:05.030 --> 00:09:09.210
Mikio-kun pushed her,
and her hand scratched him.

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:10.460
It wasn't on purpose.

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:11.610
I saw it.

00:09:11.610 --> 00:09:12.730
But she scratched me!

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:15.710
Tsumugi, did you scratch him by accident?

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:17.560
I didn't do it!

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:20.740
Mikio!

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:24.410
I heard you made another girl cry!

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:25.640
No, I didn't...

00:09:25.640 --> 00:09:27.120
Then what happened?

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.380
Please calm down!

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:32.760
I went "whoom" and she went "whoof,"

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:37.340
and her hand went "whup," 
and it scratched me...

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:39.800
So you pushed her first!

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.740
Then you need to apologize!

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:49.480
Come on. Make up.

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:52.980
I-I'm sorry.

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:53.860
No!

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:56.520
No!

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:01.840
Tsumugi, Mikio-kun is apologizing.

00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:04.450
Tsumugi-chan, listen to what he has to say.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.870
No way!

00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:18.630
Is it all right if I have a talk with her at home?

00:10:24.050 --> 00:10:25.240
I'm sorry.

00:10:28.750 --> 00:10:30.600
Tsumugi-chan, bye-bye!

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:33.880
Sorry.

00:10:33.880 --> 00:10:35.860
You can play with her next time.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:10.100
Tsumugi, there's no one 
else here but Daddy now.

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:17.630
They gave me their clay.

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:18.310
Yeah.

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:20.700
I'm not a thief.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:21.420
Yeah.

00:11:22.630 --> 00:11:24.010
I know.

00:11:24.450 --> 00:11:25.920
You're not a thief.

00:11:30.930 --> 00:11:32.870
He said something mean, huh?

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:37.050
Inuzuka Tsumugi

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:36.310
Hey,

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:40.980
why don't we buy clay and 
give it back to your friends?

00:11:40.980 --> 00:11:42.120
Why?

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:45.630
Daddy doesn't want people 
calling you a thief,

00:11:45.630 --> 00:11:48.840
even if it was a misunderstanding.

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:57.660
Okay.

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.750
Good girl.

00:12:21.410 --> 00:12:24.590
Tsumugi-chan, it's the 
long-awaited Hamburg steak day!

00:12:34.590 --> 00:12:36.590
She looks pretty down.

00:12:36.590 --> 00:12:37.480
Yes.

00:12:39.060 --> 00:12:42.020
They made up this morning, but...

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:45.280
I guess she's not totally over it.

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:51.160
So I want to use the Hamburg 
steak to cheer her up!

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:51.920
Okay!

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:53.460
Let's do our best!

00:12:55.170 --> 00:12:58.460
But it's hard to get the heat just right 
for Hamburg steak, isn't it?

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:00.570
Actually, about that...

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:01.690
Let's stew it!

00:13:01.690 --> 00:13:02.920
Stew it?

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:05.090
Stewed Hamburg steak!

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:08.350
That way you don't have to worry 
about undercooking it,

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:09.340
and it's good!

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:10.680
I see.

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:11.720
So now...

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:15.730
You're going to chop the onions.

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:17.050
Here.

00:13:17.050 --> 00:13:19.000
And here, and here.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:20.570
What's this?

00:13:20.920 --> 00:13:23.610
Apparently something awful 
happens to your eyes.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:24.990
Something awful?

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:27.430
Um... Itching? Stinging?

00:13:27.880 --> 00:13:29.880
At any rate, you need to protect your eyes.

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:33.160
But these don't really fit over my glasses...

00:13:34.370 --> 00:13:37.040
Look, she's laughing a little.

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:38.380
You're right.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:40.680
Okay, here we go.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:42.250
Yes.

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:44.970
Here we go!

00:13:47.250 --> 00:13:48.140
Um...

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:51.140
How should I chop?

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:55.020
I don't know if it'll help,

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:58.070
but my mom put it in her recipe.

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.650
How to Chop Onions

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.650
Slice in Half

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.650
First cut
from the side

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.650
Leave 
this part

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.650
Then 
turn it up

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.650
Spin it

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:02.770
So, easy, huh?

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:02.770
For the rough parts, 
hold down the edge 
of the knife like this, 
and chop them into 
little pieces, 'kay?

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:06.170
At a glance, it's hard to tell what she's saying.

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:08.740
Sorry, I think that's beyond my ability.

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:14.200
First, peel the skin off the onion,

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:19.360
and cut it in half.

00:14:21.960 --> 00:14:24.920
I'm really not feeling confident today.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:26.730
You probably shouldn't watch me cut myself.

00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:28.380
Right. I'm sorry!

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.460
First cut from the side.

00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:32.980
Leave this part.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:35.640
It's hard.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:39.940
I've got lots of band-aids, okay?

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:42.100
Then turn it up...

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.110
Spin it,

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:48.650
and cut from the top.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:52.840
It's chopped!

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:02.430
Amazing, huh?

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:03.990
It's like a magic trick, right?

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:11.800
Fry the chopped onions

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.980
until they turn a caramel color.

00:15:16.100 --> 00:15:17.850
What's a caramel color?

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.150
It's when they turn kind of 
brown and see-through,

00:15:21.150 --> 00:15:22.920
and look really yummy.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:25.940
Be careful not to burn them.

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:29.560
See? Smells good!

00:15:34.130 --> 00:15:38.400
Let's see... Moisten the bread crumbs with milk.

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:39.220
Here you go.

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:43.120
Today's Dinner Recipe

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:43.120
-Hamburg Steak

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:43.120
-Sauce

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:43.120
First, let's chop the onions. 
Cutting the onions might 
make you cry! Hang in there! 
(I've written out how to 
chop them on another page.)

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:43.120
There are fewer ingredients than I thought.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:46.620
It tastes delicious, 
but it's basically a simple dish.

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:49.660
But you can also mix in things like okra or tofu,

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:52.760
and some people even put kiwi in it.

00:15:53.190 --> 00:15:54.580
Huh...

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:58.590
The enzymes in the kiwi soften the meat

00:15:58.590 --> 00:16:00.540
and make it soft when it cooks.

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:04.300
It's just like how people put 
pineapple in sweet and sour pork.

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:08.710
Tsumugi, want to help?

00:16:10.630 --> 00:16:13.420
We're about to shape the patties.

00:16:13.420 --> 00:16:14.740
You like clay, don't you?

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:16.950
Don't want to.

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:20.570
What would make you feel better, Tsumugi?

00:16:23.280 --> 00:16:24.410
But...

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:28.380
I feel like I did something bad.

00:16:30.180 --> 00:16:32.090
You're not a thief!

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:35.000
Daddy told you he knows that!

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:37.710
That's not it.

00:16:37.710 --> 00:16:39.100
That's not it...

00:16:42.820 --> 00:16:43.850
Sensei,

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:47.360
try to listen to her more.

00:17:00.980 --> 00:17:01.860
Tsumugi.

00:17:12.290 --> 00:17:14.520
I'm not a thief,

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:17.590
but they gave me lots of clay,

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:20.760
and I didn't give it back.

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:24.220
Am I... a bad girl?

00:17:31.030 --> 00:17:32.280
Tsumugi!

00:17:32.700 --> 00:17:34.490
You're not a bad girl!

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:36.350
It's okay!

00:17:36.350 --> 00:17:37.400
It's okay.

00:17:37.400 --> 00:17:39.990
Daddy knows you're a good girl!

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:41.980
You're kind,

00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:43.690
and you do what you're told,

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:46.310
and you help around the house.

00:17:46.310 --> 00:17:48.250
And... And...

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:52.500
And you make Daddy feel so much better!

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.340
Daddy loves you!

00:18:06.760 --> 00:18:08.770
Want to make Hamburg steaks together?

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:10.560
Uh-huh.

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:19.320
So after you knead, knead, 
and knead the patty,

00:18:19.320 --> 00:18:22.920
you shape it like this,

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:26.510
and get the air out!

00:18:26.510 --> 00:18:27.430
Tsumugi!

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:29.500
Over here!

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:35.830
Good job, Tsumugi!

00:18:37.440 --> 00:18:38.360
One more time!

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:45.100
It's cooking now.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:46.860
The other side is...

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:48.320
We're stewing them after this,

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:50.310
so they just need to be browned.

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:51.640
Let's take them out!

00:18:57.460 --> 00:19:00.280
The sauce is a simple canned tomato base.

00:19:00.280 --> 00:19:02.180
Add in Worcestershire sauce,

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:03.910
and ketchup...

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.580
And lastly, a boullion cube.

00:19:09.160 --> 00:19:10.870
And now...

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:21.470
Now we just stew them, and they're done!

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:23.370
Let's add the finishing touch!

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:24.890
The finishing touch?

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.800
I-It's done!

00:19:30.800 --> 00:19:34.280
It's the best-looking thing 
we've made so far!

00:19:35.240 --> 00:19:36.730
Here you go, Tsumugi!

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:40.170
Now, time to dig in!

00:19:43.110 --> 00:19:45.060
Let's eat!

00:19:52.630 --> 00:19:54.040
Tsumugi, your hair.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:08.390
Tsumugi?

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:23.210
I'm sorry, Tsumugi.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.140
You were such a good girl the whole time.

00:20:28.040 --> 00:20:29.110
But you know...

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:32.410
No matter what kind of girl you are,

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:34.660
Daddy loves you.

00:20:40.960 --> 00:20:42.510
Yummy!

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:44.590
It's super soft!

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:46.180
Yeah. I'm glad!

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:50.880
We're amazing!

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:53.500
Today was another big success.

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:58.570
Oh, right, Tsumugi-chan.

00:20:58.570 --> 00:21:00.890
What were you trying to make with the clay?

00:21:00.890 --> 00:21:02.550
A birthday present for Daddy!

00:21:03.140 --> 00:21:04.570
A birthday present?

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:07.030
That's right! I forgot!

00:21:07.440 --> 00:21:09.640
Today's my birthday!

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:11.100
That's right!

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:15.030
It's the day with the four and two and five!

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:25.820
It's smaller now,

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:27.950
but you can have a clay Hamburg steak!

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:28.800
Really?

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:30.440
Thank you.

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:34.400
Sensei, today is your birthday?

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:37.060
That's right.

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:39.560
Tsumugi, is it good?

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:41.450
This is all I can give you right now.

00:21:39.560 --> 00:21:40.810
Yup, it's good!

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:47.530
This mixed-up part that's probably 
the best-tasting part...

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:48.890
You can have it!

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:50.280
It's my present to you!

00:21:50.280 --> 00:21:51.830
No, that's fine.

00:21:51.830 --> 00:21:53.100
I'll pass.

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:56.060
Sensei, don't say that!

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:57.480
Next time, I'll make you 
something even better!

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:57.500
Sensei!
